Theme.razor, in a Blazor Web App with `@rendermode InteractiveServer` (prerendering is on by default):

```razor
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<p>Theme: @theme</p>

@code {
    private string? theme;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        theme = await JS.InvokeAsync<string?>("localStorage.getItem", "theme");
    }
}
```

**What happens when you open the page?**

Width.razor (interactive):

```razor
@implements IDisposable
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<p>Width: @width</p>

@code {
    private DotNetObjectReference<Width>? objRef;
    private int width;

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
        {
            objRef = DotNetObjectReference.Create(this);
            await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("resizeWatcher.start", objRef);
        }
    }

    [JSInvokable]
    public void OnResize(int newWidth) => width = newWidth;

    public void Dispose() => objRef?.Dispose();
}
```

The JS calls `dotNetHelper.invokeMethodAsync("OnResize", window.innerWidth)` on every resize. You resize the window to 800 px wide. Nothing else happens on the page.

**What does the page show?**

In the project **MyShop** (assembly `MyShop`):

```csharp
public static class Prices
{
    [JSInvokable]
    public static decimal GetTax(decimal amount) => amount * 0.2m;
}
```

The JavaScript:

```js
const tax = await DotNet.invokeMethodAsync("Prices", "GetTax", 100);
```

**What happens?**

wwwroot/js/math.js:

```js
export function add(a, b) { return a + b; }
```

The component:

```csharp
protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
{
    if (firstRender)
    {
        module = await JS.InvokeAsync<IJSObjectReference>("import", "./js/math.js");
        sum = await JS.InvokeAsync<int>("add", 2, 3);
        StateHasChanged();
    }
